                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Capacity</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Mixing mechanism</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Material</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Best for</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">BlenderBottle Classic V2</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">28 oz</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Wire whisk ball</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">BPA-free plastic</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Everyday shakes</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">BlenderBottle Radian</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">26 oz</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Wire whisk ball</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Insulated stainless steel</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Cold all day, no smell</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">BlenderBottle Pro32</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">32 oz</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Wire whisk ball</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Tritan plastic</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Big, thick shakes</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">ShakeSphere Tumbler</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">24 oz</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Capsule shape, no ball</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">BPA-free plastic or steel</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">No ball to clean</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Helimix 2.0</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">28 oz</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Built-in vortex</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Plastic</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Gritty plant powders</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Ice Shaker</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">26 oz</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Removable agitator</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Insulated stainless steel</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Water bottle that mixes</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            Two numbers on every listing deserve a second look. Capacity is the volume to the brim, not the volume you can use, and most bottles' printed markings stop several ounces lower. And dishwasher-safe often means the lid only: on stainless bottles in particular, the brands recommend hand-washing the body. Neither is a reason to avoid a bottle, but both change which size and material suit you.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. The Best Protein Shaker Bottles, Ranked
          </h2>

          <p>
            These six are ranked on how well their mixing mechanism handles typical protein powders, usable capacity versus the number on the label, lid design and leak reports, cleaning and dishwasher guidance, and material. We did not run our own shake tests; mixing and leak notes summarize the manufacturer's specifications and consistent buyer reports, as explained on our <a href="/how-we-test/">how we test</a> page. Capacities and care instructions are per the brand or retailer listing at the time of writing and can differ between sizes and designs.
          </p>

