        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying by the capacity number alone</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Capacity is to the brim, and markings often stop several ounces lower. A shaker also needs headroom to mix. Fill no more than about half to two-thirds, which means a 28 oz bottle for a 12 to 16 oz shake, not a 16 oz bottle.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Shaking hot liquid in a sealed bottle</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Heat builds pressure that can pop the lid or flip cap and spray hot liquid. Mix hot drinks with a spoon or frother in an open cup, and open any foamy or fizzy shake slowly, pointed away from you.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Leaving a used bottle sealed</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Protein and milk left in a closed bottle grow bacteria and create the smell that ruins plastic shakers. Rinse immediately after drinking, then wash it fully and dry the parts separately with the lid off.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Putting stainless bottles in the dishwasher</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Brands such as BlenderBottle and Ice Shaker say lids can go on the top rack but recommend hand-washing insulated bottles to protect the vacuum insulation and finish. Wrapped or printed designs are often hand-wash only.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a cheap lookalike to save a few dollars</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Unbranded copies of popular shakers often have thinner plastic, looser threads and balls that rust. Check the listing is sold by Amazon or the brand, and that the photos show the brand's markings.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            12. Frequently Asked Questions
          </h2>

          <div class="faq-list">
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What is the best protein shaker bottle?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  For most people, the BlenderBottle Classic V2 is the best protein shaker bottle: its wire whisk ball mixes whey quickly, the screw lid and flip cap have a good leak record, and it is dishwasher safe and inexpensive. The BlenderBottle Radian is the best insulated stainless option, and the ShakeSphere Tumbler is the best if you do not want a mixing ball.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What size shaker bottle do I need?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  A 24 to 28 oz bottle suits most people, because a shaker should be filled only about half to two-thirds to mix well. That handles a 12 to 16 oz shake. Choose 20 oz for small water-only shakes and a gym bag, and 32 oz or more for thick shakes with oats, gainers or two scoops.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Why does my shaker bottle smell?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Protein and milk residue left in the bottle let bacteria grow. Rinse right after drinking, wash fully with hot soapy water and a brush, and dry the parts separately with the lid off. Soak a smelly bottle in baking soda or vinegar and water overnight. Scratched plastic may never fully recover; stainless steel usually does.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Are BlenderBottles dishwasher safe?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The plastic Classic and Pro Series bottles are described as dishwasher safe, and top-rack placement is the safer choice. Insulated stainless models such as the Radian are different: BlenderBottle says the lid can go on the top rack but recommends hand-washing the cup to preserve its finish. Check the care instructions for your specific model.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Do you need a ball in a shaker bottle?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Not strictly, but it helps. A loose wire whisk ball mixes whey, casein and plant protein faster than most alternatives. Ball-free designs such as the ShakeSphere rely on a capsule shape, and buyers report they mix well with a slightly longer shake. Cheap fixed grids are the weakest option for thick powders.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is a stainless steel shaker worth it?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  It is worth it if you carry shakes for hours, hate plastic smells or want to avoid plastic touching your drink. Double-wall steel keeps shakes cold and does not absorb odors. The trade-offs are higher price, more weight, hand-washing the bottle and not being able to see inside.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>How do I stop my shaker bottle from leaking?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Make sure the seal or gasket is in place and not twisted, screw the lid on level until it stops, and do not overfill. Avoid shaking hot or carbonated liquids in a sealed bottle, which builds pressure. If the flip cap no longer clicks shut, replace the lid or the bottle.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

          </div>
